WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:03.069
-My first guests are both Emmy
winners and two of the funniest,

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:04.871
most talented people I know.

00:00:04.871 --> 00:00:07.307
Gosh, I love them so much.
This is very exciting.

00:00:07.307 --> 00:00:10.276
They've reunited as their iconic
characters Wayne and Garth

00:00:10.276 --> 00:00:12.712
from "Wayne's World"
for a big Super Bowl commercial

00:00:12.712 --> 00:00:15.047
for Uber Eats
airing this Sunday.

00:00:15.047 --> 00:00:16.615
Look out for it.
It is really good.

00:00:16.615 --> 00:00:18.918
Here is Mike Myers
and Dana Carvey.

00:00:18.918 --> 00:00:21.420
Yeah!
-Whoo! Yeah!

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:23.022
Party on, Jimmy!
-Whoo!

00:00:23.022 --> 00:00:25.658
-Welcome, welcome, welcome
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:25.658 --> 00:00:27.427
-Yeah, we're gonna come
and get some.

00:00:27.427 --> 00:00:30.696
-Oh! Come and get some.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:30.696 --> 00:00:32.899
-Come and get some right now.
-Oh!

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:35.001
It's good to have you guys here
to come and get some.

00:00:35.001 --> 00:00:37.036
-I'm going to tour a character

00:00:37.036 --> 00:00:39.471
I call Red Redneckie
the Redneck Comedian,

00:00:39.471 --> 00:00:43.143
but I'm gonna hire
other comedians to play him.

00:00:43.143 --> 00:00:46.512
"Alright, Redneck, I'm the Red
Redneckie, Redneck Comedian.

00:00:46.512 --> 00:00:49.515
I know -- I know a redneck
married his sister,

00:00:49.515 --> 00:00:51.484
only 'cause Mama
turned him down.

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:53.052
Come and get some."

00:00:53.052 --> 00:00:55.321
"Come and get some"
is his catchphrase.

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:57.590
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.590 --> 00:00:59.391
"Come and get some."

00:00:59.391 --> 00:01:02.628
The other day --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.628 --> 00:01:05.698
"Come and get some" is
blowing up on my podcast.

00:01:05.698 --> 00:01:08.601
-Come and get some.

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:10.603
-My kids and everyone
wanted to have some food.

00:01:10.603 --> 00:01:12.638
I said, "We only have enough
hubcaps to go around

00:01:12.638 --> 00:01:15.408
to feed everybody.
Come and get some."

00:01:15.408 --> 00:01:17.877
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:18.945
You should throw
"come and get some" --

00:01:18.945 --> 00:01:20.547
-That was your turn to laugh?
-Yeah.

00:01:20.547 --> 00:01:22.649
-Is that what that is?
-Yeah, come and get some

00:01:22.649 --> 00:01:25.785
is everything. My grandpappy
invented the phrase

00:01:25.785 --> 00:01:27.220
"dollars to doughnuts."

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:29.522
Every time he got a buck,
he bought a doughnut.

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:32.258
He died at 47.
Come and get some.

00:01:32.258 --> 00:01:39.699
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.699 --> 00:01:42.335
-Dude, "come and get some"
is the best thing.

00:01:42.335 --> 00:01:43.636
-Oh, yeah!
-Oh, dude.

00:01:43.636 --> 00:01:47.806
-Whatever, whatever, whatever
crap, you don't know

00:01:47.806 --> 00:01:49.942
it gonna flersh
down that terlet.

00:01:49.942 --> 00:01:52.178
Come and get some.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:55.848
It's just bad jokes, folks.
It's not supposed to be good.

00:01:55.848 --> 00:01:58.151
-Oh, my gosh.
-Come and get some.

00:01:58.151 --> 00:01:59.352
[ Laughter ]

00:01:59.352 --> 00:02:01.587
-That's Red Redneckie
the Redneck Comedian.

00:02:01.587 --> 00:02:03.556
You can see it here
on my podcast,

00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:05.357
"Fantastic! with Dana Carvey."

00:02:05.357 --> 00:02:09.095
-Come and get some.

00:02:09.095 --> 00:02:12.432
-I have lots of questions
that I wanted to ask that

00:02:12.432 --> 00:02:13.899
I've never asked you before.
-Really?

00:02:13.899 --> 00:02:16.135
-Yeah. How long have
you known each other

00:02:16.135 --> 00:02:18.938
and what do you remember each
about meeting each other?

00:02:18.938 --> 00:02:20.740
Dana, you first?

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:24.944
-Oh. Michael and I met --
[ Laughs ]

00:02:24.944 --> 00:02:26.679
I think -- I guess it was
the late '80s.

00:02:26.679 --> 00:02:30.583
I'd done "SNL." I was fortunate
enough, freakily fortunate,

00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:31.985
to get on "Saturday Night Live,"

00:02:31.985 --> 00:02:34.286
and I was there for
a couple seasons I guess,

00:02:34.286 --> 00:02:37.256
and then our latest new
cast member appeared,

00:02:37.256 --> 00:02:38.892
and it was Mike Myers.

00:02:38.892 --> 00:02:41.260
And I liked him right away.

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:43.897
He was a very, very clever lad,
and we, you know --

00:02:43.897 --> 00:02:49.669
I think we just met around town
in the maelstrom of "SNL."

00:02:49.669 --> 00:02:53.639
Just the most intense thing you
could ever experience, I think.

00:02:53.639 --> 00:02:57.376
Mike?
-Yeah.

00:02:57.376 --> 00:02:59.612
I hadn't seen the show
'cause I lived in England

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:02.648
and it wasn't on in England,
and then I moved to Canada

00:03:02.648 --> 00:03:07.553
shortly, and I came into
what appeared to me

00:03:07.553 --> 00:03:09.956
to be like this --
and it's true --

00:03:09.956 --> 00:03:13.726
this all-star cast,
and just, like, "Oh, my God,

00:03:13.726 --> 00:03:15.294
these guys are so fantastic,"

00:03:15.294 --> 00:03:20.533
and then when I wrote
"Wayne's World,"

00:03:20.533 --> 00:03:25.271
I just thought --
I mean, you know...

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:29.342
Dana Carvey was in my sketch
because just put good people

00:03:29.342 --> 00:03:32.411
in your sketch and it'll get on,
you know, so.

00:03:32.411 --> 00:03:34.246
-Well, the first few times
we went on,

00:03:34.246 --> 00:03:35.781
we were kind of the last sketch.
-Yeah.

00:03:35.781 --> 00:03:38.050
-I think it took us a while --
so it was like --

00:03:38.050 --> 00:03:42.054
-The truth is, you were
in the area of the "SNL"

00:03:42.054 --> 00:03:44.457
on the floor, you know,
where all sketches go to die.

00:03:44.457 --> 00:03:45.792
That was where --
-Yes.

00:03:45.792 --> 00:03:47.526
-Yes.
-The one all the way

00:03:47.526 --> 00:03:49.428
far back on the left.
-Yes.

00:03:49.428 --> 00:03:51.129
-The dead corner, yeah.
-The dead corner.

00:03:51.129 --> 00:03:53.232
-That doesn't have an audience
looking at you at all.

00:03:53.232 --> 00:03:54.633
They have to watch it
on the monitor.

00:03:54.633 --> 00:03:56.135
-Yeah.
-And you're just like,

00:03:56.135 --> 00:03:58.003
"Is anybody watching?"
You feel like you're sending it

00:03:58.003 --> 00:04:00.072
out into space or something.
-Yeah. You broke the curse.

00:04:00.072 --> 00:04:02.508
-And some planet will see it.

00:04:02.508 --> 00:04:04.577
-We would jump up and down
with energy.

00:04:04.577 --> 00:04:07.046
I think when you're last up
and you're over in the corner,

00:04:07.046 --> 00:04:08.815
you're trying to be
kind of defiant.

00:04:08.815 --> 00:04:11.351
Like, we'll just bring
psychotic energy.

00:04:11.351 --> 00:04:12.852
"Wayne's --" Just screaming.

00:04:12.852 --> 00:04:15.488
But eventually it caught on.

00:04:15.488 --> 00:04:16.722
-And when you do these sketches,

00:04:16.722 --> 00:04:18.924
you don't think
it's gonna be a film.

00:04:18.924 --> 00:04:20.226
-No, we didn't think
it was gonna be a film,

00:04:20.226 --> 00:04:22.561
and then when we did it,
we didn't think necessarily

00:04:22.561 --> 00:04:24.430
they were gonna release it.
You know what I mean?

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:26.098
-Really?
-They were a little like,

00:04:26.098 --> 00:04:27.533
"Hmm, what is this?"
You remember?

00:04:27.533 --> 00:04:30.636
-Yeah, we didn't think they'd
bring actual cameras to the set.

00:04:30.636 --> 00:04:32.538
We were young. We didn't know.

00:04:32.538 --> 00:04:34.540
We weren't sure
if it was a stage play

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:37.810
or a puppet show at malls,
but anyway.

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:40.146
-But when did you feel like
it was a real movie?

00:04:40.146 --> 00:04:42.181
'Cause it was
a giant, giant movie.

00:04:43.916 --> 00:04:46.519
-That summer, I think.

00:04:46.519 --> 00:04:49.588
Dana and I were invited to
this rally

00:04:49.588 --> 00:04:56.462
that Ellen DeGeneres was hosting
at Lincoln Park in Chicago.

00:04:56.462 --> 00:05:00.399
And one of the things
that struck me was that

00:05:00.399 --> 00:05:03.202
Dana's the most relaxed
performer I'd ever --

00:05:03.202 --> 00:05:06.372
First of all, it's just,
"Let's just have fun."

00:05:06.372 --> 00:05:08.641
And I was like, "Oh, right,
we're supposed to enjoy this.

00:05:08.641 --> 00:05:11.410
You're right." Because I'm a bit
of a tortured artist at times.

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:13.012
-I think we all are.

00:05:13.012 --> 00:05:16.282
-I just wing it.
-We went out and he was like,

00:05:16.282 --> 00:05:18.951
"Just have fun. Come on.
Let's do it."

00:05:18.951 --> 00:05:21.587
And I was like, "You're not
really that person, are you?"

00:05:21.587 --> 00:05:23.155
And he is really that person,
you know what I mean?

00:05:23.155 --> 00:05:24.757
'Cause everyone always says
that, but --

00:05:24.757 --> 00:05:27.926
And I was like, "Oh, right, I
don't have to be so tortured."

00:05:27.926 --> 00:05:30.963
Still be present,
and you'd said something

00:05:30.963 --> 00:05:32.698
that got a big, giant laugh.

00:05:32.698 --> 00:05:34.733
And he was so calm that he --

00:05:34.733 --> 00:05:37.003
it was like the "ahhh"
at Lincoln Park,

00:05:37.003 --> 00:05:39.338
and he turned me and go,
"Do you want to eat at the hotel

00:05:39.338 --> 00:05:41.540
or do you want to try
and find a place in Chicago?"

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:43.009
And I'd be looking at him
like...

00:05:43.009 --> 00:05:44.476
-"We can't talk about that now!"
-"We're on stage.

00:05:44.476 --> 00:05:46.545
Don't talk to me.
What are you doing?"

00:05:46.545 --> 00:05:50.983
And he'd just wait it out
and then he'd be back in.

00:05:50.983 --> 00:05:53.318
-Isn't it fun, though? 'Cause
even though you do have fun,

00:05:53.318 --> 00:05:56.555
it is comedy, but putting all
that work into one little joke,

00:05:56.555 --> 00:05:59.392
it could take you hours.
It could take you a week

00:05:59.392 --> 00:06:01.293
to go,
"How are we gonna crack this?"

00:06:01.293 --> 00:06:04.129
And then someone has to shake
you and go, "It's comedy.

00:06:04.129 --> 00:06:05.664
Have fun." And you go,
"Right, right, right."

00:06:05.664 --> 00:06:07.333
-Come and get some.
-Come and get some.

00:06:07.333 --> 00:06:09.035
[ Laughter ]

